# What must never reach the image.
#
# There was no .dockerignore at all, and the Dockerfile ends in `COPY . .` — so every build was
# baking the local `.env` into a layer, JWT signing key and Sarvam API key included. A secret in
# a layer is a secret in every copy of that image, every registry it is pushed to and every
# `docker history` run against it, and deleting the file in a later layer does not remove it.
#
# The Drive connector made this urgent rather than merely untidy: `secrets/` holds a
# service-account key that grants access to everything shared with that account.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key

# Build context size, and correctness. The embedding, reranker and OCR models are pre-fetched
# into /app/.model_cache *before* `COPY . .`; a local cache of the same name would be copied
# over the baked one and quietly replace known-good weights with whatever is on this machine.
.model_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.git/
.github/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Local pipeline artifacts — the real ones live in MinIO.
storage_data/
*.db
*.sqlite3

# Editor and agent scratch
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
